<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sorghaghtani Beki</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1252</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sorghaghtani Beki was a Keraite princess, niece of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ong-khan">Ong Khan</a>, who married Tolui, youngest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>. After Tolui's death she managed his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and raised her four sons, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongke">Möngke</a>, Kublai, Hülegü and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ariq-boke">Ariq Böke</a>. Her alliances helped bring Möngke to the throne as great khan in 1251; she was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-east">Nestorian Christian</a> who patronised several faiths.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sorghaghtani-beki.jpg" alt="Sorghaghtani Beki" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rashid al-Din · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TuluiWithQueenSorgaqtani.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
